    "summary": "Jar. Globular with small mouth and neck and with two lug handles. Carved ribbing around shoulder and a horizontal incised ring. Made of crackled celadon glazed stoneware. The glaze stops short of the base except for a few large drops that have run down. Red body. Tubular kiln support mark on foot. Rattan handle. Raised, recessed foot. Oily substance inside it.",
